WEBVTT

00:00:08.448 --> 00:00:11.128
This time, I'm going to make sure
you stay dead!

00:00:12.288 --> 00:00:14.648
HOLLEY: You're doing brilliantly.
Now just stay focused.

00:00:14.728 --> 00:00:17.248
What's that? You want me
to head toward that ruckus?

00:00:17.328 --> 00:00:19.328
HOLLEY: No! Don't go down that street.

00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:25.648
Ohh!

00:00:30.128 --> 00:00:31.168
Hi-yah!

00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:33.688
Wow! A live karate demonstration!

00:00:33.728 --> 00:00:36.048
Stop it, Mater. Just sign off.

00:00:38.768 --> 00:00:40.208
Aaargh!

00:00:40.928 --> 00:00:41.928
(GUNSHOT)

00:00:43.248 --> 00:00:45.048
DAVID: And here they come,
the two leaders.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.448
Bumper to bumper
as they approach the finish line!

00:00:53.528 --> 00:00:55.688
-It's close!
-BRENT: Francesco's the winner!

00:00:55.768 --> 00:00:57.368
McQueen's number two.

00:00:57.488 --> 00:00:59.528
(FIREWORKS WHIZZ AND POP)

00:00:59.728 --> 00:01:02.808
That was cool!
Can I get your autograph?

00:01:03.448 --> 00:01:06.368
(CHATTER IN JAPANESE)

00:01:09.128 --> 00:01:10.568
Where'd he go?

00:01:10.728 --> 00:01:13.688
HOLLEY: Our rendezvous has been
jeopardized. Keep the device safe.

00:01:13.728 --> 00:01:17.128
-We'll be in touch.
-Dad-gum, did I miss our date?

00:01:22.528 --> 00:01:24.208
-Francesco!
-Francesco, over here.

00:01:24.288 --> 00:01:25.768
What was your strategy today?

00:01:25.888 --> 00:01:28.688
Strategia?
Francesco needs-a no strategy.

00:01:28.728 --> 00:01:29.928
It's-a very simple.

00:01:30.008 --> 00:01:34.048
You start the race, wait for Lightning
McQueen to choke, pass him, then win.

00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:36.408
Francesco always-a wins. It's-a boring.

00:01:36.528 --> 00:01:38.808
DARRELL: You were in trouble
for a while.

00:01:38.928 --> 00:01:40.848
That dirt track section
had you crawling.

00:01:40.928 --> 00:01:46.408
To truly crush one's dream, you must
first raise their hopes very high.

00:01:47.528 --> 00:01:50.408
-Mater!
-Hey, McQueen! What happened?

00:01:50.408 --> 00:01:52.528
Is the race over? You won, right?

00:01:52.608 --> 00:01:54.968
Why were you yelling at me
while I was racing?

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.928
Yelling? Oh, you thought...
That's funny right there.

00:01:59.008 --> 00:02:01.368
No, that's 'cause I seen
these two fellers doing

00:02:01.448 --> 00:02:03.528
some karate street performance.

00:02:03.608 --> 00:02:06.088
It was nutso.
One of 'em even had a flame-thrower.

00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:08.608
A flame-thrower?
What are you talking about?

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.448
-I don't understand. Where were you?
-Going to meet my date.

00:02:11.568 --> 00:02:13.128
Your date?

00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:16.288
She started talkin' to me as a voice
in my head, tellin' me where to go.

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:18.448
-What?
-Wait a minute.

00:02:18.568 --> 00:02:22.208
-I didn't screw ya up, did I?
-I lost the race because of you!

00:02:22.288 --> 00:02:24.808
Oh. I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

00:02:24.848 --> 00:02:27.888
An imaginary girlfriend?
Flame-throwers?

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:31.248
This is exactly why I don't bring you
along to these things.

00:02:31.328 --> 00:02:33.488
Maybe if I, I don't know,

00:02:33.568 --> 00:02:36.808
talk to somebody and explained
what happened, I could help.

00:02:36.848 --> 00:02:40.368
I don't need your help!
I don't want your help!

00:02:41.448 --> 00:02:43.288
REPORTER: Hey, there he is!

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:47.808
-McQueen, you had it in the bag!
-Yeah! What happened?

00:02:47.848 --> 00:02:49.488
I made a mistake.

00:02:49.608 --> 00:02:53.248
But I can assure you,
it won't happen again.

00:02:55.848 --> 00:02:59.408
Look, we know what the problem is
and we've taken care of it.

00:02:59.488 --> 00:03:01.168
(REPORTERS CALL OUT)

00:03:01.248 --> 00:03:04.488
BRENT: Lightning McQueen loses
in the last lap to Francesco Bernoulli

00:03:04.648 --> 00:03:07.088
in the first race of the World Grand Prix.

00:03:07.168 --> 00:03:10.008
And three - count 'em -
three cars flamed out

00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:13.688
leaving some to suggest that their fuel,
allinol, might be to blame.

00:03:13.848 --> 00:03:17.248
Allinol is safe. Alternative fuel is safe.

00:03:17.368 --> 00:03:20.808
There is no way my fuel
caused these cars to flame out.

00:03:20.848 --> 00:03:24.328
The jury may still be out on whether
allinol caused these accidents,

00:03:24.408 --> 00:03:25.688
but one thing's for sure,

00:03:25.848 --> 00:03:28.328
Lightning McQueen blew this race.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.048
BRENT: Team McQueen
can't be happy right now.

00:03:39.888 --> 00:03:43.528
ANNOUNCER ON PA: Welcome to
Tokyo International Airport.

00:03:52.648 --> 00:03:54.648
(ALARM WAILS)

00:04:00.888 --> 00:04:02.048
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

00:04:02.088 --> 00:04:04.968
-Come with me, please, sir.
-But I'm 'onna miss my plane.

00:04:05.048 --> 00:04:07.888
-Right this way.
-Ah, doggone it.

00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:09.848
This is about my hook, ain't it?

00:04:09.888 --> 00:04:12.848
I know I should have checked it,
but I can't, really.

00:04:12.888 --> 00:04:15.408
Look. It's attached to me.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.888
Hey, I know you. You're that feller
from the karate demonstration.

00:04:18.888 --> 00:04:21.208
I never properly introduced myself.

00:04:21.288 --> 00:04:23.688
Finn McMissile. British Intelligence.

00:04:23.768 --> 00:04:26.648
Tow Mater. Average intelligence.

00:04:26.768 --> 00:04:29.368
Who are you with? FBI? CIA?

00:04:29.448 --> 00:04:32.488
Let's just say I'm AAA affiliated.

00:04:32.568 --> 00:04:34.768
I know some karate.

00:04:34.928 --> 00:04:38.408
I don't want to brag or nuttin',
but I got me a black fan belt.

00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:41.488
-Wanna see some moves I made up?
-You're being followed.

00:04:41.568 --> 00:04:44.448
This first one,
I can reach into a car's hood

00:04:44.528 --> 00:04:47.288
pull out his battery,
and show it to him before he stalls.

00:04:47.368 --> 00:04:51.528
I call it, "What I accidentally did
to my friend Luigi once."

00:04:51.608 --> 00:04:53.328
Hey! Hi-yah-pah!

00:04:53.408 --> 00:04:55.408
-Hi-yah!
-There he is!

00:04:56.248 --> 00:04:58.248
MATER: Hi-hi-tah! Huh!

00:04:59.168 --> 00:05:01.968
Look, I probably ought to go.
I'm about to miss my flight.

00:05:02.008 --> 00:05:04.248
-Don't worry. I've taken care of that.
-Whoa!

00:05:04.328 --> 00:05:06.048
Hang on!

00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:07.128
(GRUNTS)

00:05:07.168 --> 00:05:09.368
Whoa-hah-hah!

00:05:09.448 --> 00:05:11.608
This is first-class service.

00:05:11.768 --> 00:05:14.368
You don't even have to go
through the terminal!

00:05:14.448 --> 00:05:15.808
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

00:05:15.928 --> 00:05:18.048
Your karate partners is back there.

00:05:18.128 --> 00:05:20.288
They look like
they tryin' to catch up!

00:05:20.408 --> 00:05:22.928
Drive forward.
Whatever you do, don't stop!

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.768
(TIRES SCREECH)

00:05:25.568 --> 00:05:27.808
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

00:05:37.608 --> 00:05:39.608
Whoa...

00:05:46.088 --> 00:05:47.568
Is everything okay back there?

00:05:47.648 --> 00:05:49.768
Finn, it's Sid. I'm on approach.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.528
FINN: Roger that.

00:05:53.448 --> 00:05:56.648
'Member that whole thing about me
not stoppin' no matter what?

00:06:01.848 --> 00:06:03.248
I knew I shoulda done carry-on!

00:06:03.368 --> 00:06:05.408
Thanks, old boy.

00:06:05.488 --> 00:06:07.688
-You got it, mate.
-MATER: Hey, doggonit!

00:06:07.808 --> 00:06:09.688
Look, it's my imaginary girlfriend!

00:06:09.808 --> 00:06:11.368
Come on! Get in here!

00:06:11.448 --> 00:06:15.208
I tell you what, you really do
want this first date, don't ya?

00:06:15.248 --> 00:06:17.328
That's a no-quit attitude right there.

00:06:17.408 --> 00:06:18.768
-(GUNFIRE)
-What the...?

00:06:21.648 --> 00:06:23.768
-Aargh!
-FINN: Hold on, Sid.

